{"name":"Creamy Lemon","hex":"#fff0b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"creamy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing cream.","Of food or drink, having the rich taste or thick, smooth texture of cream, whether or not it actually contains cream."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A horse with a cream-coloured coat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creamy"},{"term":"lemon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish citrus fruit.","A semitropical evergreen tree, Citrus limon, that bears such fruits."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavour/flavor and/or scent of lemons.","Of the pale yellow colour/color of lemons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Creamy","blocks":[{"text":"Creamy were a Danish-Faroese teen-pop duo, composed of Rebekka Mathew and Rannva Joensen."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creamy","wikidata":"Q5183392"},{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/33